{"name":"Savile Row","hex":"#c0b7cf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Savile Row","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A street in Mayfair, City of Westminster, London, England, known for its bespoke tailoring for men.","The tailoring companies located on Savile Row and neighbouring streets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Savile_Row"}],"entries":[{"title":"Savile Row","blocks":[{"text":"Savile Row is a street in Mayfair, central London. Known principally for its traditional bespoke tailoring for men, the street has also accommodated the headquarters of the Royal Geographical Society at 1 Savile Row, where British explorations to Africa and the South Pole were planned; and more recently, the headquarters of the Beatles' Apple Corps business at 3 Savile Row, on whose roof the band gave its final live performance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Savile_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg/330px-Savile_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savile_Row"},{"title":"Savile","blocks":[{"text":"Savile is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Arthur Savile (1819–1870), English clergyman and cricketer","David Savile, actor, married to Lois Baxter","Douglas Barton Osborne Savile (1909–2000), mycologist","Dorothy Savile, Viscountess Halifax (1640–1670)","Dorothy Savile, Countess of Burlington and of Cork (1699–1758), painter and wife of Richard Boyle, 3rd Earl of Burlington","George Savile, 1st Marquess of Halifax (1633–1695)","George Savile (disambiguation), for others of that name","Henry Savile, MP for Yorkshire","Henry Savile, MP for Yorkshire and Grantham","Henry Savile (1549–1622)","Henry Savile (politician) (1642–1687)","Jimmy Savile (1926–2011), DJ, presenter and media personality","John Savile, 1st Baron Savile of Pontefract (1556–1630), politician; M.P., Lincolnshire and Yorkshire","John Savile, 1st Baron Savile (1818–1896), British diplomat; Ambassador to Italy, 1883–1888","Leopold Halliday Savile (1870–1953), British civil engineer","Steven Savile, a British fantasy, horror and thriller writer, and editor living in Stockholm, Sweden","William Savile, 2nd Marquess of Halifax (1665–1700)"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savile"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Savile_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg/330px-Savile_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Savile_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg/330px-Savile_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaville_Row_from_Burlington_Gardens.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Savile_Row%2C_London.jpg/500px-Savile_Row%2C_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Savile_Row%2C_London.jpg/500px-Savile_Row%2C_London.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASavile_Row%2C_London.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Savile_Row_%C3%89difice_Pancarte.jpg/500px-Savile_Row_%C3%89difice_Pancarte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Savile_Row_%C3%89difice_Pancarte.jpg/1280px-Savile_Row_%C3%89difice_Pancarte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Savile_Row_%C3%89difice_Pancarte.jpg/500px-Savile_Row_%C3%89difice_Pancarte.jpg?utm_source